NextBSD local patch for vendored Apple libxml2-39.10 (libxml2 2.9.13 based)

CVE:      none assigned (upstream NEWS v2.15.3 "Security" entry; libxml2
          issue #1096, labelled Security: type confusion reading
          xmlDoc as xmlNode->properties in C14N 1.0 inclusive mode)
Upstream: 495c9451c541da25829ce321d2273da9fca72d25 (v2.15.3)
          0fd00ec5f51065340c98f084df045d76258c6bc3 (master)
          "c14n: Fix Type confusion in xmlC14NProcessAttrsAxis"
Adapted:  Verbatim one-line change, context offsets only. (The related
          xmlC14NProcessNamespacesAxis fix f879a017 / #1016 is already
          present in Apple's tree.)

diff --git a/c14n.c b/c14n.c
--- a/c14n.c
+++ b/c14n.c
@@ -1189,7 +1189,7 @@ xmlC14NProcessAttrsAxis(xmlC14NCtxPtr ctx, xmlNodePtr 
              * visible!
              */
             tmp = cur->parent;
-            while (tmp != NULL) {
+            while (tmp != NULL && tmp->type == XML_ELEMENT_NODE) {
                 attr = tmp->properties;
                 while (attr != NULL) {
                     if (xmlC14NIsXmlAttr(attr) != 0) {
